-- title:
--   K(j,j_q) lies in the fraction field of the node ring
-- statement:
--   Fix a prime $q$, a valuation subring $A$ of $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ (an algebraic closure of $\mathbb Q$), a field $k$, a ring homomorphism $\mathrm{red} : A \to k$, an element $a \in k$, and an intermediate field $K$ of $\overline{\mathbb Q}/\mathbb Q$. Let $x$ be a Laurent series over $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ lying in `fieldOver (1 * q) K`, that is, in the subfield of $\overline{\mathbb Q}((\mathfrak q))$ generated by the constant series attached to the elements of $K$ together with the two series `jqModC` (the $q$-expansion $1/\mathfrak q + \cdots$ of $j$, written as $\mathfrak q^{-1}$ times the power series $j_{\mathrm{num}}$ with coefficients cast into $\overline{\mathbb Q}$) and `jqNModC` at level $1 \cdot q$ (its substitution $\mathfrak q \mapsto \mathfrak q^{1\cdot q}$). Then there exist Laurent series $y, z$ with $z \neq 0$ and $x z = y$, both $y$ and $z$ belonging to `modularLocalizedAtPoint (1 * q) (coeffSubring A K) (redRestrict red K) a (a ^ q)`: the subring of those $f$ for which there are two-variable polynomials $r, s$ with coefficients in $A \cap K$ such that $f \cdot s(j, j_q) = r(j, j_q)$ (coefficients being sent to constant series) while the value of $s$ at $(a, a^q)$, coefficients reduced by $\mathrm{red}$ restricted to $A \cap K$, is nonzero.
--
--   This is the elementary half of the statement that $K(j, j_q)$ is the fraction field of the local ring of the plane model of $X_0(q)$ at the point $(a, a^q)$, over the subring $A \cap K$; no hypothesis is imposed on $a$. It supplies the fraction-field input for the statements about places and normalisation of that local ring, including the existence and uniqueness of places centred at $0$ and at $1728$ attached to a crossing presentation.
-- source:
